.TH SSCG "8" "March 2026" "sscg 4.0.3" "System Administration Utilities"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
sscg \- Tool for generating x.509 certificates
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B sscg
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR...]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display the
version number
and exit.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite any
pre\-existing
files in the
requested
locations.
DANGER: You
probably don't
want to use
this!
.SS "Help options:"
.TP
\-?, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help
message
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\fR
Display brief
usage message
.PP
Verbosity options
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Display no
output unless
there is an
error.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Display
progress
messages.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable logging
of debug
messages.
Implies
verbose.
Warning! This
will print
private key
information to
the screen!
.PP
Certificate Subject options
.TP
\fB\-\-lifetime\fR=\fI\,1\-3650\/\fR
Certificate
lifetime
(days).
(default: 398)
.TP
\fB\-\-country\fR=\fI\,US\/\fR, CZ, etc.
Certificate DN:
Country (C).
(default: "US")
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR=\fI\,Massachusetts\/\fR, British Columbia, etc.
Certificate DN:
State or
Province (ST).
.TP
\fB\-\-locality\fR=\fI\,Westford\/\fR, Paris, etc.
Certificate DN:
Locality (L).
.TP
\fB\-\-organization\fR=\fI\,My\/\fR Company
Certificate DN:
Organization
(O). (default:
"Unspecified")
.TP
\fB\-\-organizational\-unit\fR=\fI\,Engineering\/\fR, etc.
Certificate DN:
Organizational
Unit (OU).
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR=\fI\,myname\/\fR@example.com
Certificate DN:
Email Address
(Email).
.TP
\fB\-\-hostname\fR=\fI\,server\/\fR.example.com
The valid
hostname of the
certificate.
Must be an
FQDN. (default:
current system
FQDN)
.TP
\fB\-\-subject\-alt\-name\fR alt.example.com
Optional
additional
valid hostnames
for the
certificate. In
addition to
hostnames, this
option also
accepts
explicit values
supported by
RFC 5280 such
as
IP:xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx May be specified multiple times.
.PP
Certificate Key Cryptography Options
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-type=\fR{rsa,ecdsa,mldsa}
Type of key to
use for the
certificate
private keys.
(default: rsa)
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-strength\fR=\fI\,2048\/\fR or larger
Strength of the
certificate
private keys in
bits. This
argument is
only valid if
\fB\-\-key\-type\fR is
set to rsa.
(default: 2048)
.TP
\fB\-\-ec\-curve=\fR{secp224r1,secp256r1,secp384r1,secp521r1}
EC curve to use
for the
certificate
private keys.
This argument
is only valid
if \fB\-\-key\-type\fR
is set to ecdsa.
.TP
\fB\-\-mldsa\-nist\-level=\fR{2,3,5}
NIST level to
use for the
ML\-DSA key.
This argument
is only valid
if \fB\-\-key\-type\fR
is set to
mldsa.
(default: 2)
.TP
\fB\-\-hash\-alg=\fR{sha256,sha384,sha512}
Hashing
algorithm to
use for signing
RSA and ECDSA
keys. This
argument is
only valid if
\fB\-\-key\-type\fR is
rsa or ecdsa.
(default:
"sha256")
.TP
\fB\-\-cipher\-alg=\fR{des\-ede3\-cbc,aes\-256\-cbc}
Cipher to use
for encrypting
key files.
(default:
"aes\-256\-cbc")
.PP
Certificate Authority File Options
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where the
public CA
certificate
will be stored.
(default:
"./ca.crt")
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-mode\fR=\fI\,0644\/\fR
File mode of
the created CA
certificate.
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-key\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where the
CA's private
key will be
stored. If
unspecified,
the key will be
destroyed
rather than
written to the
disk.
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-key\-mode\fR=\fI\,0600\/\fR
File mode of
the created CA
key.
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-key\-password\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Provide a
password for
the CA key
file. Note that
this will be
visible in the
process table
for all users,
so it should be
used for
testing
purposes only.
Use
\fB\-\-ca\-keypassfile\fR or \fB\-\-ca\-key\-password\-prompt\fR for secure password entry.
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-key\-passfile\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
A file
containing the
password to
encrypt the CA
key file.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-ca\-key\-password\-prompt\fR
Prompt to enter
a password for
the CA key file.
.PP
Certificate Revocation List File Options
.TP
\fB\-\-crl\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where an
(empty)
Certificate
Revocation List
file will be
created, for
applications
that expect
such a file to
exist. If
unspecified, no
such file will
be created.
.TP
\fB\-\-crl\-mode\fR=\fI\,0644\/\fR
File mode of
the created
Certificate
Revocation List.
.PP
Service Certificate File Options
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where the
public service
certificate
will be stored.
(default
"./service.pem")
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-mode\fR=\fI\,0644\/\fR
File mode of
the created
certificate.
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-key\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where the
service's
private key
will be stored.
(default
"service\-key.pem")
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-key\-mode\fR=\fI\,0600\/\fR
File mode of
the created
certificate key.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-cert\-key\-password\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Provide a
password for
the service key
file. Note that
this will be
visible in the
process table
for all users,
so this flag
should be used
for testing
purposes only.
Use
\fB\-\-cert\-keypassfile\fR or \fB\-\-cert\-key\-password\-prompt\fR for secure password entry.
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-key\-passfile\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
A file
containing the
password to
encrypt the
service key
file.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-cert\-key\-password\-prompt\fR
Prompt to enter
a password for
the service key
file.
.PP
Client Authentication Certificate File Options
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where a
client
authentication
certificate
will be stored.
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-mode\fR=\fI\,0644\/\fR
File mode of
the created
certificate.
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-key\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Path where the
client's
private key
will be stored.
(default is the
client\-file)
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-key\-mode\fR=\fI\,0600\/\fR
File mode of
the created
certificate key.
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-key\-password\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Provide a
password for
the client key
file. Note that
this will be
visible in the
process table
for all users,
so this flag
should be used
for testing
purposes only.
Use
\fB\-\-client\-keypassfile\fR or \fB\-\-client\-key\-password\-prompt\fR for secure password entry.
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-key\-passfile\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
A file
containing the
password to
encrypt the
client key file.
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-key\-password\-prompt\fR
Prompt to enter
a password for
the client key
file.
.PP
Diffie\-Hellman Parameter File Options
.TP
\fB\-\-dhparams\-file\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
A file to
contain a set
of
Diffie\-Hellman
parameters.
(Default: not
created)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhparams\-named\-group\fR=\fI\,STRING\/\fR
Output
well\-known DH
parameters. The
available named
groups are:
ffdhe2048,
ffdhe3072,
ffdhe4096,
ffdhe6144,
ffdhe8192,
modp_2048,
modp_3072,
modp_4096,
modp_6144,
modp_8192,
modp_1536,
dh_1024_160,
dh_2048_224,
dh_2048_256.
(Default:
"ffdhe4096")
.TP
\fB\-\-dhparams\-generator=\fR{2,3,5}
The generator
value for
dhparams.
(default: 2)
